Huh, yummy?

00:08:57.824 --> 00:08:58.657
Okay, good.

00:08:58.657 --> 00:08:59.490
Time to eat.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:02.462
We're going to show you
how Lily eats her ketchup.

00:09:02.462 --> 00:09:04.469
- [Lily] You're going to find
out I have a lot of weird--

00:09:04.469 --> 00:09:05.794
- [Evan] She opens the ketchup pack

00:09:05.794 --> 00:09:08.243
and then dips the ketchup in.

00:09:08.243 --> 00:09:09.671
- [Lily] No mess!

00:09:09.671 --> 00:09:12.535
Guys, you got to use
your creativity, guys.

00:09:12.535 --> 00:09:14.393
- [Aleks] What's the
alternative way to eating it,

00:09:14.393 --> 00:09:16.233
that you think it will make a mess?

00:09:16.233 --> 00:09:19.600
- Like, spilling it all over the place.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.395
And then, different food
touches different foods.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:25.240
- [Evan] Aleks is very intrigued.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.526
How's the poutine?

00:09:27.526 --> 00:09:28.359
- [Lily] You should try it out!

00:09:28.359 --> 00:09:29.192
- It's not bad!

00:09:29.192 --> 00:09:30.025
The gravy's not so great, though.

00:09:30.025 --> 00:09:30.858
I'll be honest.

00:09:30.858 --> 00:09:32.485
- [Nina] Can I try one?

00:09:32.485 --> 00:09:33.468
- [Evan] She's going to say, oh yeah,

00:09:33.468 --> 00:09:35.635
I hear what you're saying.

00:09:37.687 --> 00:09:39.855
- It's different poutine taste.

00:09:39.855 --> 00:09:41.474
- [Aleks] Yeah.

00:09:41.474 --> 00:09:42.464
- Tastes a little burnt.

00:09:42.464 --> 00:09:43.297
- [Aleks] Exactly.

00:09:43.297 --> 00:09:44.870
- We're all going to the
Tony Robbins conference

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.442
for two reasons.

00:09:46.442 --> 00:09:49.839
One is, hopefully, to
improve ourselves, to learn.

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:53.679
The reason why I picked these guys, what,

00:09:53.679 --> 00:09:56.030
was they were the first ones, at TDS,

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.941
to embrace their one word, and find it.

00:09:58.941 --> 00:10:00.108
So, Nina is...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.778
- What?
- What's your one word?

00:10:02.778 --> 00:10:04.270
- Oh, kids.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.235
- Lily is...
- Extraordinary.

00:10:06.235 --> 00:10:07.909
- Edwin is...
- Together.

00:10:07.909 --> 00:10:09.082
- [Evan] And Aleks is...

00:10:09.082 --> 00:10:10.623
- Belong.

00:10:10.623 --> 00:10:13.358
- So, I wanted to reward them,
and take them to go see Tony.

00:10:13.358 --> 00:10:15.146
And, hopefully, he can
share some insights,

00:10:15.146 --> 00:10:18.046
to help all of us become
better versions of ourselves.

00:10:18.046 --> 00:10:19.796
Also, we're teachers.

00:10:20.798 --> 00:10:22.575
And I wanted to learn from Tony.

00:10:22.575 --> 00:10:25.601
And we teach three hours at
night, three different classes.

00:10:25.601 --> 00:10:29.842
Tony's on stage for, like,
eight, ten, 12 hours at a time.

00:10:29.842 --> 00:10:30.793
And I was hopin' that, maybe,

00:10:30.793 --> 00:10:32.146
we could learn something from him,

00:10:32.146 --> 00:10:34.426
that we could bring to
our classes as well,

00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:36.275
to be better instructors.

00:10:36.275 --> 00:10:37.834
So, we'll see.

00:10:37.834 --> 00:10:39.015
I'm excited to learn from him.

00:10:39.015 --> 00:10:40.902
So, we're going to go around the room,

00:10:40.902 --> 00:10:44.045
and find out one thing that
everybody is hoping to learn

00:10:44.045 --> 00:10:45.656
from this session in LA.

00:10:45.656 --> 00:10:46.489
- I don't know.

00:10:46.489 --> 00:10:49.071
I've been thinking, lately,

00:10:49.071 --> 00:10:50.657
there are things that I always want to do,

00:10:50.657 --> 00:10:51.879
and I will just think about it.

00:10:51.879 --> 00:10:52.778
I don't do it.

00:10:52.778 --> 00:10:55.089
So, I was thinking I
should just go for it.

00:10:55.089 --> 00:10:56.360
I shouldn't think too long.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.592
Take action, right away.

00:10:58.592 --> 00:10:59.701
Take actions.

00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:00.534
- [Evan] Boom!

00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:02.287
- There's actually several
things I want to work on.

00:11:02.287 --> 00:11:05.145
But, the most important thing is that

00:11:05.145 --> 00:11:09.312
I feel like my outside
does not reflect my inside.

00:11:10.953 --> 00:11:13.223
Like, inside, I feel like a beast!

00:11:13.223 --> 00:11:17.595
And the outside, I'm
more like a goat, maybe.

00:11:17.595 --> 00:11:18.801
(Evan imitating goat noise)
Right?

00:11:18.801 --> 00:11:20.139
Yeah, like a small goat!

00:11:20.139 --> 00:11:23.579
So, I really, really
feel like I just need to

00:11:23.579 --> 00:11:25.698
manifest what's inside of me.

00:11:25.698 --> 00:11:27.572
There's something holding me back.

00:11:27.572 --> 00:11:28.405
- [Evan] Beast mode!

00:11:28.405 --> 00:11:29.346
- I don't know what it is.

00:11:29.346 --> 00:11:30.196
I need to find out.

00:11:30.196 --> 00:11:31.029
- [Evan] I like it.

00:11:31.029 --> 00:11:33.223
- [Edwin] I think I want
to be able to tap into

00:11:33.223 --> 00:11:35.713
the reason why I chose my one word.

00:11:35.713 --> 00:11:39.963
And be able to have it
reflect it off my every day,

00:11:39.963 --> 00:11:41.913
a lot like Lily's tapping the beast,

00:11:41.913 --> 00:11:44.824
and wanting to be able to tap into that,

00:11:44.824 --> 00:11:47.324
and share it, 24/7.

00:11:48.304 --> 00:11:49.654
- [Evan] I love it, yes!

00:11:49.654 --> 00:11:51.784
- [Aleks] So, what's the one
thing that I want to work on?

00:11:51.784 --> 00:11:54.652
I want to work on being a
better leader, for everyone,

00:11:54.652 --> 00:11:55.485
and a better example.

00:11:55.485 --> 00:11:57.180
I think I'm holding myself back.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.932
I'm holding myself back, because
a lot of limiting beliefs,

00:11:59.932 --> 00:12:02.108
procrastination and a bunch of things.

00:12:02.108 --> 00:12:02.941
And it frustrates me,

00:12:02.941 --> 00:12:05.318
because I can be playing at
a higher level, and I'm not.

00:12:05.318 --> 00:12:07.158
So, I'm hoping to find
some answers about myself.

00:12:07.158 --> 00:12:08.749
- [Evan] Yeah, boom!

00:12:08.749 --> 00:12:12.360
For me, I'm most excited
for the experience.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.364
I surround myself with this
kind of content, daily.

00:12:15.364 --> 00:12:16.632
And there is nobody else that I would

00:12:16.632 --> 00:12:18.455
really want to go and meet.

00:12:18.455 --> 00:12:20.008
There's nobody I want to
meet, like one-on-one,

00:12:20.008 --> 00:12:21.059
and pick their brain.

00:12:21.059 --> 00:12:22.156
But, I'm excited to go

00:12:22.156 --> 00:12:25.294
and just be a part of the experience.

00:12:25.294 --> 00:12:28.986
And I'm not necessarily looking
for any one thing, I'm open.

00:12:28.986 --> 00:12:31.294
I'm open to being surprised.

00:12:31.294 --> 00:12:33.659
And I want to feel it.

00:12:33.659 --> 00:12:34.890
I want to see how Tony does it.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.642
And I want to see what comes from him.

00:12:36.642 --> 00:12:37.484
- [Lily] Nice.

00:12:37.484 --> 00:12:39.835
- That's what I got.

00:12:39.835 --> 00:12:43.071
And I want my hair rubbed.
(Nina laughing)

00:12:43.071 --> 00:12:44.792
Mission accomplished.

00:12:44.792 --> 00:12:47.622
Lily also wants Tony to
put his hand on her head.

00:12:47.622 --> 00:12:50.145
- Yeah, I want to feel small for once.

00:12:50.145 --> 00:12:51.875
I mean, I want to unleash the beast,

00:12:51.875 --> 00:12:53.895
but at the same time,
physically, I want to feel small.

00:12:53.895 --> 00:12:54.728
It's weird!

00:12:54.728 --> 00:12:55.793
(Aleks and Edwin conversing)

00:12:55.793 --> 00:12:56.710
I have a lot of limiting beliefs!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.236
(Evan laughing)

00:12:58.236 --> 00:12:59.986
